<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vatican Radio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1931–</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vatican Radio is the broadcasting service of the Holy See, set up by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guglielmo-marconi">Guglielmo Marconi</a> and inaugurated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-xi">Pope Pius XI</a> on 12 February 1931. Run for most of its history by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>, it broadcasts in dozens of languages worldwide. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> it carried news and papal messages to listeners in occupied and communist countries.</p></div>
